<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}" class="no-js">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  {%- comment -%}
    Flipped before first paint so progressive-enhancement fallbacks — the
    cart's "Update cart" button, for one — can be hidden without flashing on
    screen first. Inline and synchronous on purpose; deferring it defeats it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>document.documentElement.className = document.documentElement.className.replace('no-js', 'js');</script>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  {%- comment -%}
    color_primary was never a setting on this theme — the palette is authored
    as ink/accent/paper/gingham/surface — so this rendered as an empty
    attribute and mobile browsers fell back to their own chrome colour.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <meta name="theme-color" content="{{ settings.color_ink | default: '#0C2340' }}">

  <title>
    {{ page_title }}
    {%- if current_tags %} &ndash; {{ current_tags | join: ', ' }}{% endif %}
    {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; Page {{ current_page }}{% endif %}
    {%- unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless %}
  </title>

  {%- if page_description -%}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">

  {%- comment -%}
    Nearly all of this shop's traffic arrives from a link pasted into
    Instagram, a group chat, or Facebook. Without these, every one of those
    links unfurls as a bare URL with no picture and no price. Product pages
    describe the product; everything else describes the shop.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if template.name == 'product' -%}
    {%- assign og_type  = 'product' -%}
    {%- assign og_title = product.title -%}
    {%- assign og_desc  = product.description | strip_html | truncate: 200 -%}
    {%- assign og_image = product.featured_media | image_url: width: 1200 -%}
  {%- elsif template.name == 'collection' and collection -%}
    {%- assign og_type  = 'website' -%}
    {%- assign og_title = collection.title -%}
    {%- assign og_desc  = collection.description | strip_html | truncate: 200 -%}
    {%- assign og_image = collection.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200 -%}
  {%- elsif template.name == 'article' and article -%}
    {%- assign og_type  = 'article' -%}
    {%- assign og_title = article.title -%}
    {%- assign og_desc  = article.excerpt_or_content | strip_html | truncate: 200 -%}
    {%- assign og_image = article.image | image_url: width: 1200 -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign og_type  = 'website' -%}
    {%- assign og_title = page_title | default: shop.name -%}
    {%- assign og_desc  = page_description | default: shop.description -%}
    {%- assign og_image = settings.share_image | image_url: width: 1200 -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ shop.name | escape }}">
  <meta property="og:type" content="{{ og_type }}">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ og_title | escape }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical_url }}">
  {%- if og_desc != blank -%}
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ og_desc | escape }}">
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if og_image != blank -%}
    <meta property="og:image" content="https:{{ og_image }}">
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ og_title | escape }}">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
  {%- else -%}
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
  {%- endif -%}
  <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ og_title | escape }}">
  {%- if og_desc != blank -%}
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ og_desc | escape }}">
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if template.name == 'product' -%}
    <meta property="og:price:amount" content="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | divided_by: 100.0 }}">
    <meta property="og:price:currency" content="{{ cart.currency.iso_code }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  {{ content_for_header }}

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Assistant:wght@400..700&family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght,SOFT,WONK@0,9..144,400..700,0..100,0..1;1,9..144,400..700,0..100,0..1&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

  {%- comment -%}
    The tab icon comes from artwork the shop actually owns, or it doesn't
    render at all. There was a hand-authored SVG here — a mark invented to
    fill the slot, not drawn by the person whose shop this is — and inventing
    a brand mark is not the theme's job. Upload one under Theme settings and
    it appears; leave it empty and the browser shows its own default, which is
    honest in a way a made-up logo isn't.

    Still not logo.png: that file is 1.2 MB, and serving it raw made every
    page load fetch a full-resolution logo to paint a 16px icon.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
    <link rel="icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 96 }}">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 180 }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  {{ 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  {%- comment -%}
    Was `{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url | script_tag }}` at the foot of <body>.
    script_tag emits a plain, parser-blocking <script>, and sitting at the
    bottom meant the browser only discovered the file after parsing the whole
    document. In the head with defer it downloads alongside the HTML and still
    executes after the DOM is built — which is what the bottom placement was
    buying, so nothing here depends on running earlier.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

  {%- comment -%}
    Five authored colors come from the theme editor; every other token is
    derived from them with Liquid colour filters so the palette can never
    drift out of step with itself. `default` guards against a setting that
    has been cleared — an empty custom property resolves to `unset` and
    would take the colour with it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign c_ink     = settings.color_ink     | default: '#0C2340' -%}
  {%- assign c_accent  = settings.color_accent  | default: '#E87722' -%}
  {%- assign c_paper   = settings.color_paper   | default: '#FBF7EF' -%}
  {%- assign c_gingham = settings.color_gingham | default: '#A8C4E0' -%}
  {%- assign c_surface = settings.color_surface | default: '#FFFFFF' -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Whatever sits ON an accent fill has to be chosen, not assumed. Auburn
    orange is light enough that white fails at 2.96:1 and ink wins at 5.33:1,
    but a darker school colour flips that — cardinal or crimson need white,
    and ink on cardinal would be dark-on-dark. Measure both and take the
    better one, so changing the accent in the theme editor to another
    school's colour stays readable without touching the stylesheet.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign contrast_on_white = c_accent | color_contrast: '#FFFFFF' -%}
  {%- assign contrast_on_ink   = c_accent | color_contrast: c_ink -%}
  {%- if contrast_on_ink > contrast_on_white -%}
    {%- assign c_on_accent = c_ink -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign c_on_accent = '#FFFFFF' -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  <style>
    :root {
      --font-heading: 'Fraunces', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
      --font-heading-weight: 500;
      --font-heading-style: normal;
      --font-body: 'Assistant', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      --font-body-weight: 400;
      --font-body-style: normal;

      /* Authored */
      --color-ink:     {{ c_ink }};
      --color-accent:  {{ c_accent }};
      --color-paper:   {{ c_paper }};
      --color-gingham: {{ c_gingham }};
      --color-surface: {{ c_surface }};

      {%- comment -%}
        Blend toward paper rather than lightening. color_lighten raises HSL
        lightness while holding saturation, so a saturated navy lightens into
        a vivid blue (#0C2340 at +32 gives #266EC9) instead of the soft slate
        you actually want. Mixing carries the ink toward the page instead.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      /* Derived */
      --color-bg:            {{ c_paper }};
      --color-bg-alt:        {{ c_ink | color_mix: c_paper, 5 }};
      --color-bg-deep:       {{ c_ink }};
      --color-surface-warm:  {{ c_ink | color_mix: c_paper, 3 }};

      --color-text:          {{ c_ink }};
      --color-text-muted:    {{ c_ink | color_mix: c_paper, 65 }};

      --color-primary:       {{ c_accent }};
      --color-primary-hover: {{ c_accent | color_darken: 10 }};
      --color-primary-light: {{ c_accent | color_lighten: 38 }};
      --color-secondary:     {{ c_ink }};

      {%- comment -%}
        Auburn orange carries white text at only 2.96:1 and sits on paper as
        small text at 2.77:1 — both under AA. Orange fills keep the true
        colour and take navy text; orange that IS text uses this darker cut.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      --color-accent-ink:    {{ c_accent | color_darken: 22 }};
      /* Chosen by measurement above — see the comment on c_on_accent. */
      --color-on-accent:     {{ c_on_accent }};

      /* Warm accent reads on the navy surfaces; gingham carries the borders.
         These were the same hex under two names before — now each means one thing. */
      --color-accent-warm:   {{ c_accent | color_lighten: 18 }};
      --color-border:        {{ c_ink | color_mix: c_paper, 12 }};
      --color-border-warm:   {{ c_gingham }};
      --color-gingham-soft:  {{ c_gingham | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.55 }};

      {%- comment -%}
        Scrims and shadows were hardcoded rgba espresso and terracotta in
        theme.css, left over from the identity this shop replaced — so they
        were the one part of the palette that ignored the theme editor
        entirely. Tinted with the authored ink and accent, they follow a
        colour change like everything else.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Paper at strength, for the bands that run on ink. Same story as the
        scrims: these were a warm white from the previous identity, so the
        announcement bar, the centred hero, and the newsletter all ignored the
        authored paper colour.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      --on-dark-strong: {{ c_paper | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.85 }};
      --on-dark:        {{ c_paper | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.82 }};
      --on-dark-muted:  {{ c_paper | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.65 }};
      --on-dark-line:   {{ c_paper | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.50 }};
      --on-dark-faint:  {{ c_paper | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.40 }};
      --on-dark-border: {{ c_paper | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.18 }};
      --on-dark-hover:  {{ c_paper | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.10 }};
      --on-dark-fill:   {{ c_paper | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.08 }};

      --color-header-bg:   {{ c_paper  | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.94 }};
      --color-accent-glow: {{ c_accent | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.22 }};

      --color-scrim:      {{ c_ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.45 }};
      --color-scrim-soft: {{ c_ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.38 }};
      --shadow-sm:     0 1px 4px  {{ c_ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.07 }};
      --shadow-md:     0 4px 20px {{ c_ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.10 }};
      --shadow-lg:     0 12px 48px {{ c_ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.14 }};
      --shadow-warm:   0 8px 32px {{ c_accent | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.18 }};
      --shadow-header: 0 2px 16px {{ c_ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.09 }};
      --shadow-sticky: 0 -4px 24px {{ c_ink | color_modify: 'alpha', 0.09 }};

      /* .container reads --max-width, so wire the Layout setting to it. */
      --max-width: {{ settings.page_width | default: 1280 }}px;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body
  class="template-{{ template.name | handle }} cards--{{ settings.product_image_shape | default: 'pin' }}{% if settings.enable_animations %} animations-enabled{% endif %}"
  data-money-format="{{ shop.money_format | strip_html | escape }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    theme.js had /cart.js, /cart/add.js, /cart/change.js and /collections/all
    written into it directly. Those paths gain a locale or market prefix on a
    shop that adds one, and a hardcoded copy in a .js asset can't see it — the
    routes object can, so the paths are handed over here instead.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  data-cart-url="{{ routes.cart_url }}"
  data-cart-add-url="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"
  data-cart-change-url="{{ routes.cart_change_url }}"
  data-all-products-url="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
>

  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>

  {% section 'announcement-bar' %}
  {% section 'header' %}

  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {% section 'footer' %}

  {%- comment -%}
    Starts inert so its Close/Checkout/View-cart controls aren't in the tab
    order of every page while the drawer sits off-screen. theme.js lifts it on
    open and puts it back on close.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div id="cart-drawer" class="cart-drawer" aria-hidden="true" inert>
    <div class="cart-drawer__overlay"></div>
    <div class="cart-drawer__panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Shopping cart">
      <div class="cart-drawer__header">
        <h2 class="cart-drawer__title">Your Cart</h2>
        <button class="cart-drawer__close btn-icon" aria-label="Close cart">
          <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="cart-drawer__body" id="cart-drawer-body">
        <div class="cart-drawer__empty">
          <p>Your cart is empty.</p>
          <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="btn btn--outline btn--sm">Browse the buttons</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cart-drawer__footer" id="cart-drawer-footer" hidden>
        <div class="cart-drawer__subtotal">
          <span>Subtotal</span>
          <span id="cart-drawer-subtotal"></span>
        </div>
        <p class="cart-drawer__note">Shipping & taxes calculated at checkout</p>
        <a href="/checkout" class="btn btn--primary btn--full">Checkout</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" class="btn btn--outline btn--full">View full cart</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</body>
</html>
